docs/MC/RetroCommander.exe

# ── SINTRAN / ND-500 run artifacts dropped in the REPO ROOT by the test harnesses ──
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: `git status` at this root was 894 lines, 864 of them untracked emulator
# output (.TXT/.DATA/.PROG/.SYMB/...). That is not untidiness - it actively endangers the
# shared-tree rule. Two sessions work in this one checkout and the rule is "stage only your
# exact files, never `git add -A`". A 900-line status makes that rule impossible to verify by
# eye and makes an accidental sweep of another session's work-in-progress much likelier.
# Measured 2026-08-28; see AI-FRICTION-REVIEW-2026-08-28.md finding N3.
#
# EVERY PATTERN IS ROOT-ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING.
# `.DATA`, `.LABE` and `.TEXT` are also the extensions of the MICROCODE GROUND TRUTH -
# docs/MC/MICRO-5800-B30.DATA, docs/MC/5800-30.TEXT and friends, which are tracked and are the
# source GROUND-TRUTH.md points every carve at. A bare `*.DATA` would hide new ones. The
# leading slash confines each pattern to this directory only, so docs/MC/ is untouched.
# Verified before writing: no tracked file lives at the repo root except .md, LICENSE and
# the dotfiles (`git ls-files | grep -v /`).
#
# If you ever need to keep one of these at the root, `git add -f <path>` still works.

/*.TXT
/*.DATA
/*.LABE
/*.TEST
/*.EXT
/*.SYMB
/*.PROG
/*.BRF
/*.LIST
/*.MODE
/*.BPUN
/*.OUT
/*.DOM
/*.PSEG
/*.DSEG
/*.NRF
/*.DEFS
/*.VTM
/*.BATC
/*.PLNC
/*.INCL
/*.IMPT
/*.ERR
/*.XCOM
/*.CNFG
/*.PLIB
/*.T
/A.T
/.SYMB
